WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.500
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar and you're watching Mind Your Decisions

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Here's a fun problem given to elementary school students in China:

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.000
How tall is the table based on the following pictures?

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
I adapted this problem from a tweet by China Focus.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.500
Can you figure it out?

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:27.860
Give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for a solution.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.000
[3]

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.500
[2]

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.000
[1]

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.960
So one way to solve this problem is to use algebra.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.500
The first picture, we can translate into the following equation:

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:58.000
We have the height of the cat plus the height of the table minus the height of the turtle is equal to 170.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.500
The second picture will correspond to the equation:

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:07.000
The height of the turtle plus the height of the table minus the height of the cat is equal to 130.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.500
So now from these two equations, we need to solve for the height of the table.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:19.500
There's a neat little trick we can do - we can add these two equations together.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.000
The variables of cat and turtle will then cancel out.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:31.040
So we have two times table is equal to 170 plus 130 which is 300

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:35.000
and therefore table is equal to 150

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.500
so the height of the table is a hundred and fifty centimeters.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.000
That's one way we can solve the problem.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:45.500
Now there's also a clever way if you think visually:

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:51.000
Imagine stacking these two pictures on top of each other.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.560
Now notice the height from the top of the cat at the bottom

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:58.000
to the top of the cat at the top is equal to

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.060
130 plus 170 which is 300.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.500
We can then erase the animals from the picture

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:10.000
And then we can rearrange it and we can clearly see

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.000
that the height of two tables is 300

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:17.000
So the height of one table will be 150 centimeters.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:19.760
Did you figure it out?

